Yep, this is common. I tend to start a character in "suicide mode" unless
he's really exceptional in some way. I drink from all fountains, never
bother running away, etc, until I get an edge. My current game features a
tourist who got a wish from a fountain two spaces from the level 1 up
ladder. (contrary to public opinion, I wished for a named weapon; tends
to help more at very low levels than GDSM 'cause monsters never get to
hit you.)

Wierdly enough, my first 3.1.3 character nearly ascended (archon on the
air level - but I didn't go out without a fight!) and my third did. Both
were wizards with some wicked starting magic - I can't remember what.

>"All great nethack stories end in death."
